stafford aven district council is  currently consulting on a site  allocations plan  following on from the video about sua2  and sua4  there are four new site specific  proposals in and on the edges stratfor  upon avon which have been put forward  this video goes into a little bit of  detail about each one  proposal sua 5 lies east of shipston  road  the site comprises three hectares of  land immediately south of the roseburg  retail park  it has been identified to provide a  suitable opportunity for specific  businesses  currently operating on wharf road in the  town to relocate  this in turn will allow that part of the  canal quarter regeneration zone to be  redeveloped  and therefore help to deliver a key  component of the core strategy  as the site isn't identified in the  course strategy and is greenfield in  nature  it is necessary for the site allocations  plan to establish the principle of such  a development  the site is reasonably well related to  the physical form of the town  given its proximity to the retail park  and the two recent developments  comprising older people's accommodation  it will be necessary to ensure that the  immunity of adjacent residential  properties is not unduly affected  by the proposed business development  a legal agreement will be required to  ensure the occupation of the site is  restricted to specific named companies  relocated from the canal quarter  the exception to this is the scope for  small business units to be provided  there is a close relationship between  the canal quarter this site and reserve  housing site  str b identified in the plan the  district council  accepts that scrb may need to act as  enabling development  as such any viability issues will need  to be independently assessed to justify  the release of strb for this purpose  then we've got proposal s2a6  stratford-upon-avon gateway  this area incorporates henley street  windsor street arden street and green  hill street  in the centre of the town while it is  expected that most of the existing  uses will remain the proposal provides  for the redevelopment of specific parts  of the area for a range of appropriate  uses  these include visitor attractions and  accommodation  retail and other commercial uses offices  leisure  community and residential  the rejuvenation of the area will need  to comprise high quality buildings and  public realm  the historic fabric of the conservation  area is listed buildings  will need to be protected and enhanced  it would also provide scope for  additional walking routes through the  area  such as between arden street and windsor  street  there is an opportunity to create a  specific gateway feature on the approach  to the historic core of the town  possibly at the junction of birmingham  road and arden street  similarly there is scope for green hill  street to provide a more attractive  route into the town centre from the  railway station  it is intended that some sort of concept  plan will be produced  to guide the future enhancement of the  whole area  proposal scua 7 frother street slash  grove road  this is another part of the central area  of the town that is need in need of  rejuvenation  again it is stressed that there is no  exception that existing uses should be  redeveloped  however there are opportunities for new  uses to be provided  and as the recent hotels division shows  a range of commercial community and  residential would be appropriate  there may be scope to redevelop all or  parts of the public  car park in conjunction with  stratford-upon-avon town council  it will be necessary to retain listed  buildings and those of  local historical significance  proposal sua 8 stafford upon avon  college  the capacity of stratford-upon-avon  secondary school on ulster road is now  very limited  and there is no scope to provide  additional accommodation  on its existing site an opportunity has  arisen for the school to utilize  adjacent land owned by stratfor college  this is currently used as a car park but  is now supplies to requirements  war russia county council has now  acquired this land for the school to use  it is understood it will remain as a car  park but this will  release land within the school campus  for additional buildings  in any case the land is prone to  flooding which is a major constraint for  development  i hope this has helped explain these  four sites remember you can find out  more in the site allocations plan  and submit any comments you have by  visiting our website at  www.stratford.gov dot uk  forward slash zappo
 

